# Keychron keyboards (USB vendor 3434).
#
# kanata reads the physical keyboard directly (via /dev/input/event*) to
# re-emit it through /dev/uinput. By default those event nodes are root:input
# and the primary user is not in the `input` group.
#
# Instead of group membership (which on Fedora Atomic is awkward: `input`
# lives in /usr/lib/group via NSS `altfiles`, so `usermod -aG input` is a
# no-op), tag the devices with `uaccess`. systemd-logind then grants the
# active local session user an ACL on the node — the same mechanism that
# already makes /dev/uinput writable.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ENV{ID_VENDOR_ID}=="3434", ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}=="1", TAG+="uaccess"
